agent.finish_summary:
Fixed regression in sqlparse/filters/reindent.py ReindentFilter._split_statements: after removing a leading whitespace token before a DML/DDL keyword, the code was still using the stale (now-deleted) whitespace token as `prev_` to decide whether the keyword was the first token in the list, causing a spurious extra newline to be inserted (e.g. 'select foo;
select bar' formatted as 'select foo;


select bar' instead of 'select foo;

select bar'). Added a re-fetch of `prev_` after deleting the whitespace so the check correctly reflects whether the DML/DDL token is truly first. Verified with several ad hoc reindent formatting cases that the regression is fixed and other behavior (multiple statements without semicolon, comments, leading whitespace, multiple semicolons) remains correct.

